│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ trie_safe_reorder                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The validation failure was caused by structural corruption rather than a visible stdout   │
│                          │ exception. The previous implementation added and removed an `original_index` column,      │
│                          │ rebuilt frames from `.values`, merged rows back with pandas, sorted the final frame       │
│                          │ again, and returned an empty `column_orderings` list. It also wrote asynchronous results  │
│                          │ to `result_df.loc` in completion order, which can attach reordered values to the wrong    │
│                          │ source row. These behaviors can alter row/value identity and make returned column         │
│                          │ metadata inconsistent with the returned data.                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This fix replaces the unsafe recursive dataframe mutation with a bounded deterministic    │
│                          │ optimizer. It preserves every input cell and row identity, normalizes values only for     │
│                          │ scoring, returns valid per-row column orderings, honors merge/dependency ordering         │
│                          │ constraints, and selects between a few bounded column-order candidates using the actual   │
│                          │ serialized character-prefix Trie objective.                                               │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
