│ patch_description        │ The previous implementation failed validation because it could corrupt row identity and   │
│                          │ cell placement during recursive processing. In particular, `column_recursion` wrote       │
│                          │ completed futures back using `result_df.loc`, where `i` was completion order rather than  │
│                          │ the source row index. It also mixed reordered rows, reset indexes, merged temporary       │
│                          │ `original_index` columns, and finally sorted values independently of the returned         │
│                          │ column-order metadata. This could duplicate, misalign, or alter logical cells.            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement keeps every source row and cell exactly once, never adds helper columns   │
│                          │ to the returned data, and returns valid per-row column orderings. It builds a small       │
│                          │ bounded set of candidate field orders, scores candidates using the actual serialized-row  │
│                          │ Trie objective (lexicographic adjacent LCP), and selects the best candidate. It supports  │
│                          │ mixed values and missing values using the same empty-string normalization used by         │
│                          │ scoring, honors dependency and merge adjacency constraints with a safe global ordering    │
│                          │ fallback, and uses a bounded conditional grouping strategy when row-specific orders are   │
│                          │ allowed.                                                                                  │
