│ patch_name               │ trie_safe_reorder                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The original implementation corrupts rows during recursion: `as_completed()` returns      │
│                          │ futures in arbitrary order but writes them using a sequential `i`, losing the source-row  │
│                          │ mapping. It also adds/removes an `original_index` column, merges dataframes after         │
│                          │ row-specific column permutations, returns an empty ordering list, and finally sorts       │
│                          │ values independently of the reported per-row column layout. These behaviors can alter row │
│                          │ identity and violate validation invariants.                                               │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This replacement preserves every original cell, row, column, index, and shape. It builds  │
│                          │ bounded candidate column layouts using serialized cell values, scores candidates with the │
│                          │ exact sorted-string adjacent-LCP Trie objective, and returns valid per-row column         │
│                          │ orderings. It supports mixed values and missing values without modifying stored values,   │
│                          │ honors merge groups as contiguous column blocks, and applies one-way dependency ordering  │
│                          │ where possible.                                                                           │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
