│ patch_description        │ The validation failure is caused by the original recursive implementation corrupting row  │
│                          │ placement and column identity. In particular, `as_completed()` returns futures in         │
│                          │ arbitrary order but writes results using `result_df.loc`, so rows are assigned to         │
│                          │ unrelated positions. The implementation also creates temporary frames without preserving  │
│                          │ indexes or dtypes, appends an `original_index` cell into the reorderable content,         │
│                          │ conditionally changes schemas, and finally sorts mixed-type values directly. These        │
│                          │ operations can duplicate, reorder incorrectly, or alter cells, which violates validation  │
│                          │ requirements.                                                                             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement keeps every source row, value, index, and column count intact. It         │
│                          │ normalizes values only for prompt-scoring estimates, constructs bounded candidate         │
│                          │ column-order strategies, evaluates them using sorted serialized-row LCP reuse, and        │
│                          │ returns the best valid row-specific ordering. No evaluator state is accessed and no       │
│                          │ temporary identity column is inserted into the returned data.                             │
