│ patch_description        │ The original implementation could corrupt row identity and cell placement:                │
│                          │ `as_completed()` returned rows in arbitrary order but wrote them using sequential `loc`,  │
│                          │ intermediate DataFrames discarded original indexes, and the method ultimately returned an │
│                          │ empty `column_orderings` list despite reordering columns. It also used value-based        │
│                          │ recursion and merge operations that could alter the layout instead of preserving every    │
│                          │ original cell.                                                                            │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This fix replaces the unsafe recursive mutation path with bounded candidate construction. │
│                          │ It preserves every source value, supports mixed types and missing values, returns valid   │
│                          │ column ordering metadata for every output row, honors merge groups as contiguous          │
│                          │ column-order constraints and one-way dependencies as ordering constraints, and chooses    │
│                          │ among a small set of candidates using the actual serialized-string Trie/LCP objective.    │
