│                          │ indices, rebuilt frames from raw `.values.tolist()`, changed column layouts,              │
│                          │ appended/dropped `original_index`, merged rows back through pandas, and finally returned  │
│                          │ an empty column-ordering list. It also optimized squared cell-length statistics and       │
│                          │ adjacent operations rather than the evaluator's serialized character-prefix objective.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This replacement keeps every original value, row, column, and shape intact. It builds a   │
│                          │ bounded set of candidate column-order strategies, measures each using the exact sorted    │
│                          │ serialized-row LCP objective, and returns the best valid row permutation plus matching    │
│                          │ per-row column orderings. Missing values are normalized only for scoring, never written   │
│                          │ back into the output data.                                                                │
