│ patch_type               │ fix                                                                                       │
│ patch_name               │ trie_safe_reorder                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The original implementation failed validation because it could corrupt row identity and   │
│                          │ column/value alignment: it added and removed an `original_index` column, merged           │
│                          │ dataframes, rebuilt rows from `.values.tolist()`, returned empty column orderings, and    │
│                          │ finally sorted mixed-type data using all columns. It also relied on attribute access for  │
