│ patch_name               │ trie_safe_reorder                                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The original implementation could corrupt row identity and column placement during        │
│                          │ recursive reconstruction. In particular, it wrote completed futures into `result_df.loc`  │
│                          │ in completion order rather than source-row order, rebuilt frames from `.values.tolist()`  │
│                          │ without preserving labels or indexes, appended and later merged an `original_index`       │
│                          │ helper column, and finally returned an empty column-ordering list. Those behaviors        │
│                          │ violate the required API and can cause validation failures even when shapes happen to     │
│                          │ match.                                                                                    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ The replacement keeps every original value, row, index, and column exactly once. It       │
│                          │ computes serialized values only for scoring heuristics, evaluates a bounded set of        │
│                          │ candidate column layouts using the exact sorted-string LCP objective, and returns valid   │
│                          │ column orderings. It supports global layouts, merge/dependency constraints, mixed values, │
│                          │ missing values, and row-specific conditional layouts without mutating source cells.       │
